<title>USA: Xomed Surgical Q4 oper shr profit $0.16.</title>
<headline>Xomed Surgical Q4 oper shr profit $0.16.</headline>
<dateline>JACKSONVILLE, Fla 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Oper shr profit	  $0.16     loss	 $0.05</p>
<p> Oper net profit	  1,235     loss	    15</p>
<p> Net sales		 16,876		   16,188</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   7,024		    4,617</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Oper shr loss	    $0.46     loss	 $0.03</p>
<p> Oper net loss	    1,167   profit	   325</p>
<p> Net sales		 65,664		   59,865</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   5,238		    4,617</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name is Xomed Surgical Products Inc.</p>
<p>1994 and 1995 Q4 are pro forma due to April 1996 acquisition, changes in the company's capital structure, and October 1996 payment of preferred dividends on formerly outstanding preferred stock.</p>
<p>1996 oper net includes $2.4 million no-cash write-off of acquired research and development related to April 1996 acquisition of TreBay Medical Corp and $1.9 million restructuring charge in 1996 Q2.</p>
<p>1995 oper net includes $551,000 for amortization of acquisition costs allocated to inventory from its acquisition of Xomed-Treace in April 1994.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
